fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC4292473"]},"doi":"10.1128/aem.03099-14","title":"Substrate-induced radical formation in 4-hydroxybutyryl coenzyme A dehydratase from Clostridium aminobutyricum.","authorString":"Zhang J, Friedrich P, Pierik AJ, Martins BM, Buckel W.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Zhang J","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Jin","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratorium für Mikrobiologie, Fachbereich Biologie and Synmikro, Philipps-Universität, Marburg, Germany Max-Plank-Institut für terrestrische Mikrobiologie, Marburg."}]}},{"fullName":"Friedrich P","lastName":"Friedrich","firstName":"Peter","initials":"P","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratorium für Mikrobiologie, Fachbereich Biologie and Synmikro, Philipps-Universität, Marburg, Germany Max-Plank-Institut für terrestrische Mikrobiologie, Marburg."}]}},{"fullName":"Pierik AJ","lastName":"Pierik","firstName":"Antonio J","initials":"AJ","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1509-6370"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institut für Zytobiologie, Philipps-Universität, Marburg, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Martins BM","lastName":"Martins","firstName":"Berta M","initials":"BM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Institut für Biologie, Strukturbiologie/Biochemie, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, Berlin, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Buckel W","lastName":"Buckel","firstName":"Wolfgang","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Laboratorium für Mikrobiologie, Fachbereich Biologie and Synmikro, Philipps-Universität, Marburg, Germany Max-Plank-Institut für terrestrische Mikrobiologie, Marburg buckel@staff.uni-marburg.de."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1509-6370"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"81","journalIssueId":2242843,"dateOfPublication":"2015 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2015,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Appl Environ Microbiol","title":"Applied and environmental microbiology","essn":"1098-5336","issn":"0099-2240","isoabbreviation":"Appl Environ Microbiol","nlmid":"7605801"},"printPublicationDate":"2015-02-01"},"pubYear":"2015","pageInfo":"1071-1084","abstractText":"4-Hydroxybutyryl-coenzyme A (CoA) dehydratase (4HBD) from Clostridium aminobutyricum catalyzes the reversible dehydration of 4-hydroxybutyryl-CoA to crotonyl-CoA and the irreversible isomerization of vinylacetyl-CoA to crotonyl-CoA. 4HBD is an oxygen-sensitive homotetrameric enzyme with one [4Fe-4S](2+) cluster and one flavin adenine dinucleotide (FAD) in each subunit. Upon the addition of crotonyl-CoA or the analogues butyryl-CoA, acetyl-CoA, and CoA, UV-visible light and electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) spectroscopy revealed an internal one-electron transfer to FAD and the [4Fe-4S](2+) cluster prior to hydration. We describe an active recombinant 4HBD and variants produced in Escherichia coli. The variants of the cluster ligands (H292C [histidine at position 292 is replaced by cysteine], H292E, C99A, C103A, and C299A) had no measurable dehydratase activity and were composed of monomers, dimers, and tetramers. Variants of other potential catalytic residues were composed only of tetramers and exhibited either no measurable (E257Q, E455Q, and Y296W) hydratase activity or <1% (Y296F and T190V) dehydratase activity. The E455Q variant but not the Y296F or E257Q variant displayed the same spectral changes as the wild-type enzyme after the addition of crotonyl-CoA but at a much lower rate. The results suggest that upon the addition of a substrate, Y296 is deprotonated by E455 and reduces FAD to FADH·, aided by protonation from E257 via T190. In contrast to FADH·, the tyrosyl radical could not be detected by EPR spectroscopy. FADH· appears to initiate the radical dehydration via an allylic ketyl radical that was proposed 19 years ago. The mode of radical generation in 4HBD is without precedent in anaerobic radical chemistry. It differs largely from that in enzymes, which use coenzyme B12, S-adenosylmethionine, ATP-driven electron transfer, or flavin-based electron bifurcation for this purpose.","affiliation":"Laboratorium für Mikrobiologie, Fachbereich Biologie and Synmikro, Philipps-Universität, Marburg, Germany Max-Plank-Institut für terrestrische Mikrobiologie, Marburg.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Clostridium","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Escherichia coli","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Free Radicals","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Acyl Coenzyme A","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Acetyl Coenzyme A","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Flavin-Adenine Dinucleotide","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Hydro-Lyases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","d